feat(strip): typed letters refine selection; Ctrl+Space picks; bigger UI

- Typing letters (or backspacing) right after the trigger no longer
  dismisses the strip: controller.refine(typed) selects the first
  candidate whose text starts with the prefix (case-insensitive).
  Whitespace, trigger chars, or a non-matching prefix end the beat as
  before. Amends hard rule 2 accordingly.
- Ctrl+Space inserts the selected entry; Alt+1..0 and click still work.
  planPick gains a `typed` parameter so picks replace the typed prefix
  with the full candidate ("Paris is th" + pick "the" -> "Paris is the ").
- Strip renders the selection (is-selected highlight, text-normal) and
  is a bit bigger (font-smallest -> font-smaller, opacity 0.9).

